   "text": {
    "L1": "A fair test changes only one thing: the thing we are testing.",
    "L2": "Everything else stays the same, so we can tell what caused the result.",
    "L3": "For a cloth test, change only the type of cloth. Keep its size, water, place and hanging time the same.",
    "L4": "Measure how long each cloth takes to dry, and record the results in a table with clear headings and units.",
    "L5": "A result should be an observation or measurement, not an opinion such as good or nice.",
    "L6": "Repeat the test because one try could be a mistake or happen by chance.",
    "L7": "Now choose the plan that changes only the cloth type."
   },
